{"question":"For salaries 100, 200, and NULL, which rows survive WHERE salary <> 100, and why?","answer":"For salaries 100, 200, and NULL, the WHERE clause salary <> 100 returns only the row with 200 because the comparison for 100 yields FALSE and the comparison for NULL yields UNKNOWN, both of which are filtered out.","insufficient":false,"citations":[{"sectionId":"null-where","quote":"SQL uses TRUE, FALSE, and UNKNOWN in its three-valued logic. A WHERE clause keeps a row only when its predicate is TRUE; FALSE and UNKNOWN are both filtered out. For salaries 100, 200, and NULL, WHERE salary <> 100 returns only the row with 200. To include missing salaries, write salary <> 100 OR salary IS NULL."},{"sectionId":"null-comparison","quote":"NULL represents missing or unknown information. It is not zero, an empty string, or a value equal to another NULL. Ordinary SQL comparisons involving NULL, including NULL = NULL and NULL <> 5, evaluate to UNKNOWN rather than TRUE or FALSE. Use IS NULL or IS NOT NULL to test missingness."}],"mode":"support-reviewed","model":"qwen3.5:9b","elapsedMs":25786,"sources":[{"id":"null-where","page":1,"title":"WHERE keeps only TRUE","text":"SQL uses TRUE, FALSE, and UNKNOWN in its three-valued logic. A WHERE clause keeps a row only when its predicate is TRUE; FALSE and UNKNOWN are both filtered out. For salaries 100, 200, and NULL, WHERE salary <> 100 returns only the row with 200. To include missing salaries, write salary <> 100 OR salary IS NULL.","textZh":"SQL 使用 TRUE、FALSE、UNKNOWN 三值逻辑。WHERE 仅保留条件为 TRUE 的行。工资为 100、200、NULL 时，salary <> 100 只返回 200。要包含缺失工资，使用 salary <> 100 OR salary IS NULL。","score":0.7078946176426791,"semantic":0.7216372679680166,"lexical":0.6666666666666666},{"id":"null-logic","page":2,"title":"Combining unknown conditions","text":"In SQL three-valued logic, NOT UNKNOWN is UNKNOWN. TRUE OR UNKNOWN is TRUE, FALSE OR UNKNOWN is UNKNOWN, FALSE AND UNKNOWN is FALSE, and TRUE AND UNKNOWN is UNKNOWN. Thus NOT (salary = 100) still excludes rows with NULL salary in a WHERE clause.","textZh":"NOT UNKNOWN 仍为 UNKNOWN。TRUE OR UNKNOWN 为 TRUE，FALSE OR UNKNOWN 为 UNKNOWN，FALSE AND UNKNOWN 为 FALSE，TRUE AND UNKNOWN 为 UNKNOWN。因此 NOT (salary = 100) 仍会过滤 NULL。","score":0.6290897051755804,"semantic":0.6721196069007738,"lexical":0.5},{"id":"null-not-in","page":3,"title":"The NOT IN trap","text":"x NOT IN (1, NULL) behaves like x <> 1 AND x <> NULL. For x = 2 the result is TRUE AND UNKNOWN, which is UNKNOWN. For x = 1 the result is FALSE. No row passes WHERE x NOT IN (1, NULL). To avoid unexpected exclusion, remove NULL from the list or use an appropriate correlated NOT EXISTS condition.","textZh":"x NOT IN (1, NULL) 等价于 x <> 1 AND x <> NULL。x 为 2 时结果是 UNKNOWN，为 1 时结果为 FALSE，因此没有行能通过 WHERE。可移除列表中的 NULL，或使用适当的关联 NOT EXISTS。","score":0.618441924080337,"semantic":0.6857003432182271,"lexical":0.4166666666666667},{"id":"null-count","page":2,"title":"Counting rows versus values","text":"COUNT(*) counts all rows. COUNT(column) counts only rows where that column is not NULL. AVG(column) ignores NULL values rather than treating them as zero. For scores 10, 20, NULL: COUNT(*) = 3, COUNT(score) = 2, SUM(score) = 30 and AVG(score) = 15.","textZh":"COUNT(*) 计算全部行数。COUNT(列) 仅计算该列不为 NULL 的行。AVG 忽略 NULL，不把它当成零。10、20、NULL 的行数为 3，非空数为 2，总和为 30，平均值为 15。","score":0.5517769581991154,"semantic":0.596813722043265,"lexical":0.4166666666666667},{"id":"null-comparison","page":1,"title":"NULL is not a value","text":"NULL represents missing or unknown information. It is not zero, an empty string, or a value equal to another NULL. Ordinary SQL comparisons involving NULL, including NULL = NULL and NULL <> 5, evaluate to UNKNOWN rather than TRUE or FALSE. Use IS NULL or IS NOT NULL to test missingness.","textZh":"NULL 表示缺失或未知信息。它不是零、空字符串，也不等于另一个 NULL。普通比较只要涉及 NULL（包括 NULL = NULL），结果就是 UNKNOWN。请用 IS NULL 或 IS NOT NULL 判断缺失。","score":0.5062145246236067,"semantic":0.6193971439425867,"lexical":0.16666666666666666}],"attempts":[{"attempt":1,"